1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:24,000
Shen He: We tried a store-wide half-price day once. The shop was packed that day, and then almost none of those people ever came back. We haven't run a discount like that since.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Lu Yao: Welcome to Shop Notes. I'm Lu Yao. My guest today is Shen He, who founded Half Acre Books, and we're talking about how an independent bookstore lives on members and events.

3
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Lu Yao: Shen He, how did Half Acre Books get started?

4
00:01:20,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Shen He: We opened in Hangzhou in 2019. It's 120 square meters, with about 8,000 titles on the shelves. There are 4 of us now, 2 full time. I just wanted a place where people would sit down and read.

5
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Lu Yao: What was hardest in those first two years?

6
00:03:25,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Shen He: 2020 was quiet, so we tried to push it with a "clearance day", everything half price. It was busy, sure. But most people picked only the discounted books, paid and left.

7
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Lu Yao: Why didn't they come back?

8
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Shen He: They came for the discount, not for the shop. When the discount stopped, so did their reason to come.

9
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Lu Yao: So in 2021 you started a membership. How did you set up the annual pass?

10
00:07:00,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Shen He: It's 399 yuan a year. 10% off books all year, one coffee a month, and the book club is free. We didn't want to hold on to people with discounts. We wanted them to have a reason to come back every month.

11
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Lu Yao: How many members do you have now?

12
00:09:30,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Shen He: 620 at the end of last year, and 71% renewed. That's from our membership system's export. Nobody has audited it.

13
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Lu Yao: How much of your revenue comes from membership fees?

14
00:11:35,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Shen He: In 2025, membership fees were 12%. Books are still half, coffee is 30%, and events are 8%.

15
00:12:30,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Lu Yao: A quick ad. This episode is sponsored by ShopTally, a phone bookkeeping app for small shops. You record every sale and every expense on your phone, and every evening it sends you a summary of the day. I've used it for three months, and the daily summary saves me the evening reconciliation. Listeners get the first month free with the code SHOPNOTES at example.com/shoptally.

16
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Lu Yao: Back to the shop. How did the Thursday book club start?

17
00:14:00,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Shen He: Every Thursday night, 20 seats. Members come free, everyone else pays 39 yuan, and that includes a drink. At first five or six people came. Now it's often full.

18
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Lu Yao: The tickets don't make money on their own. Why run it every week?

19
00:17:25,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Shen He: People who come to the book club often leave with a book. It's really a reason to come back every week.

20
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Lu Yao: How heavy is the rent?

21
00:20:45,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Shen He: 18,000 yuan a month. It's our biggest cost, so every square meter has to earn its place.

22
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:45,000
Lu Yao: If you started over, what would you do less of?

23
00:21:50,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Shen He: No store-wide discounts. I've heard half of Hangzhou's independent bookstores have closed in the last few years. I haven't counted. But I know we're still here, and it isn't because we're cheap.

24
00:24:35,000 --> 00:25:05,000
Lu Yao: Then why is it?

25
00:25:10,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Shen He: Because some people want to come back every month. The membership, the book club, a cup of coffee: they're all reasons to come back.

26
00:28:40,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Lu Yao: One piece of advice for listeners who want to open a shop?

27
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:55,000
Shen He: Work out why someone would walk into your shop, and why they'd come back next month.

28
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:40,000
Lu Yao: Thank you, Shen He. This is Shop Notes, I'm Lu Yao. If this episode helped, send it to a friend who's opening a shop. See you next time.
